# testdata
#
# testdata/ holds real private project files and is never committed. The one
# exception is the Go fuzzing corpus: `go test -fuzz` writes a reproducer to
# testdata/fuzz/<Target>/ when it finds a crash, and that reproducer is the
# regression test. Without this exception a crash found by fuzzing could never
# be committed.
# Note the trailing /* rather than a bare testdata/: git cannot re-include a
# path whose parent directory is itself excluded, so an exception under a
# `testdata/` rule would silently never match.
testdata/*
!testdata/fuzz/

# The zlib level-1 golden vectors for internal/zlib1. Every case is either
# synthetic or taken from a committed fixture, so no private data is
# involved; see testdata/README.md.
!testdata/zlib1/

# Exception: the Employees-* fixtures are ours, not private data. They were
# generated with the ComponentAce DB Manager and all hold the same synthetic
# Employees table (three invented rows), so they carry no private data and
# no vendor material -- only the format's own ABS0LUTEDATABASE/ABSP magic. One
# per encryption algorithm, they are committed because they are the only
# fixtures CI can use: without them every fixture-backed test skips on a runner
# and the crypto is never exercised at all.
# Keep this list explicit, one filename per line; never widen it to a glob,
# which could silently catch a private fixture.
!testdata/Employees-Rijndael_128.abs
!testdata/Employees-Rijndael_256.abs
!testdata/Employees-DES_Single.abs
!testdata/Employees-DES_Triple.abs
!testdata/Employees-Blowfish.abs
!testdata/Employees-Twofish_128.abs
!testdata/Employees-Twofish_256.abs
!testdata/Employees-Square.abs
